      "icon": "💡",
      "title": "4. Input Tax Credit (ITC)",
      "content": "**Input Tax Credit** means: if you are a business, you can **subtract** the GST you already paid on purchases (inputs) from the GST you collect on sales (output).\n\n**Formula:**\nGST Payable = Output GST − Input GST\n\n**Example:**\nA shopkeeper buys goods for ₹1,000 + 18% GST = ₹180 (input GST).\nHe sells them for ₹1,500 + 18% GST = ₹270 (output GST).\nGST payable to government = 270 − 180 = **₹90**.\n\nThis avoids the **cascading effect** (tax on tax) that existed before GST."
    },
