      "title": "5. Common Mistakes",
      "content": "**Mistake 1:** Calculating GST on the total price instead of the base price.\n→ GST is always on the **pre-tax price**, not the final amount.\n\n**Mistake 2:** Confusing the total GST rate with CGST/SGST rates.\n→ If GST = 12%, then CGST = 6% and SGST = 6%. Don't apply 12% twice!\n\n**Mistake 3:** Forgetting to add both CGST and SGST to get the total.\n→ Total tax = CGST + SGST (for intra-state) or just IGST (for inter-state).\n\n**Mistake 4:** Mixing up input and output tax in ITC questions.\n→ Input = what you paid; Output = what you collected."
